<p id=3D"mwSQ">The purpose of a web browser is to fetch content and display=
 it on the user's device.<sup about=3D"#mwt21" class=3D"mw-ref reference" i=
d=3D"cite_ref-5" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=
=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;=
:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-5&quot;}}"><a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-5" id=3D"mwSg"><span clas=
s=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwSw"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwTA">=
[</span>5<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwTQ">]</span></span></a></sup>=
 This process begins when the user inputs a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_Resource_Locator" title=3D"Uniform Re=
source Locator" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwTg">Uniform Resource Locator<=
/a> (URL), such as <i id=3D"mwTw"><code id=3D"mwUA"><span typeof=3D"mw:Nowi=
ki" id=3D"mwUQ">https://en.wikipedia.org/</span></code></i>, into the brows=
er's <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Address_b=
ar" title=3D"Address bar" id=3D"mwUg">address bar</a>. Virtually all URLs o=
n <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_W=
eb" title=3D"World Wide Web" id=3D"mwUw">the Web</a> start with either <i i=
d=3D"mwVA"><code id=3D"mwVQ">http:</code></i> or <i id=3D"mwVg"><code id=3D=
"mwVw">https:</code></i> which means they are retrieved with the <a rel=3D"=
mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP" title=3D"HTTP" id=
=3D"mwWA">Hypertext Transfer Protocol</a> (HTTP). For <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink=
" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTPS" title=3D"HTTPS" id=3D"mwWQ">=
secure mode</a> (HTTPS), the connection between the browser and <a rel=3D"m=
w:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_server" title=3D"Web =
server" id=3D"mwWg">web server</a> is <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encryption" title=3D"Encryption" id=3D"mwWw">encryp=
ted</a>, providing a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Communications_security" title=3D"Communications security" id=3D"mwX=
A">secure</a> and <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Information_privacy" title=3D"Information privacy" id=3D"mwXQ">private<=
/a> data transfer.<sup about=3D"#mwt24" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"ci=
te_ref-6" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&qu=
ot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;=
id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-6&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-6" id=3D"mwXg"><span class=3D"mw-=
reflink-text" id=3D"mwXw"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwYA">[</span>=
6<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwYQ">]</span></span></a></sup> For thi=
s reason, a web browser is often referred to as an HTTP client<sup about=3D=
"#mwt27" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-7" rel=3D"dc:references"=
 typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&=
quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-tex=
t-cite_note-7&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser=
#cite_note-7" id=3D"mwYg"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwYw"><span=
 class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwZA">[</span>7<span class=3D"cite-bracket" i=
d=3D"mwZQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=3D"#mwt30" class=3D"mw-ref r=
eference" id=3D"cite_ref-8" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/re=
f" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;=
body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-8&quot;}}"><a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-8" id=3D"mwZg">=
<span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwZw"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=
=3D"mwaA">[</span>8<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwaQ">]</span></span>=
</a></sup> or a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/User_agent" title=3D"User agent" id=3D"mwag">user agent</a>. Requisite ma=
terials, including text, <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Style_sheet_(web_development)" title=3D"Style sheet (web develop=
ment)" id=3D"mwaw">style sheets</a>, <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Images" title=3D"Images" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D=
"mwbA">images</a>, and other types of <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Website#Multimedia_and_interactive_content" title=
=3D"Website" id=3D"mwbQ">multimedia</a>, are <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downloaded" title=3D"Downloaded" class=3D"mw=
-redirect" id=3D"mwbg">downloaded</a> from the server. Once the materials h=
ave been downloaded, the web browser's <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title=3D"Browser engine" id=3D"mwb=
w">engine</a> (also known as a layout engine or rendering engine) is respon=
sible for converting those resources into an interactive visual representat=
ion of the page on the user's device.<sup about=3D"#mwt33" class=3D"mw-ref =
reference" id=3D"cite_ref-behindscene_9-0" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"=
mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&=
quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;behindscene&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id=
&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-behindscene-9&quot;}}"><a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-behindscene-9" id=3D"mw=
cA"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwcQ"><span class=3D"cite-bracket=
" id=3D"mwcg">[</span>9<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwcw">]</span></s=
pan></a></sup> Modern web browsers also contain separate <a rel=3D"mw:WikiL=
ink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JavaScript_engine" title=3D"Java=
Script engine" class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwdA">JavaScript engines</a> whi=
ch enable more complex interactive applications inside the browser.<sup abo=
ut=3D"#mwt36" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-howBlinkWorks_10-0"=
 rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&q=
uot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;howBlinkWork=
s&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note=
-howBlinkWorks-10&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_bro=
wser#cite_note-howBlinkWorks-10" id=3D"mwdQ"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text=
" id=3D"mwdg"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwdw">[</span>10<span clas=
s=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mweA">]</span></span></a></sup> A web browser that=
 does not render a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Graphical_user_interface" title=3D"Graphical user interface" id=3D"mwe=
Q">graphical user interface</a> is known as a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Headless_browser" title=3D"Headless brows=
er" id=3D"mweg">headless browser</a>.</p>

<p id=3D"mwew">Web pages usually contain <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperlink" title=3D"Hyperlink" id=3D"mwfA">hyper=
links</a> to other pages and resources. Each link contains a URL, and when =
it is <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_an=
d_click" title=3D"Point and click" id=3D"mwfQ">clicked</a> or <a rel=3D"mw:=
WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touchscreen" title=3D"Touch=
screen" id=3D"mwfg">tapped</a>, the browser navigates to the new resource. =
Most browsers use an internal <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Web_cache" title=3D"Web cache" id=3D"mwfw">cache</a> of web=
 page resources to improve loading times for subsequent visits to the same =
page. The cache can store many items, such as large images, so they do not =
need to be downloaded from the server again. Cached items are usually only =
stored for as long as the web server stipulates in its HTTP response messag=
es.<sup about=3D"#mwt39" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-11" rel=
=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;=
:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quo=
t;mw-reference-text-cite_note-11&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-11" id=3D"mwgA"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-tex=
t" id=3D"mwgQ"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwgg">[</span>11<span cla=
ss=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwgw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=3D"#mwt=
42" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-12" rel=3D"dc:references" typ=
eof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot=
;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-ci=
te_note-12&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#ci=
te_note-12" id=3D"mwhA"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwhQ"><span c=
lass=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwhg">[</span>12<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=
=3D"mwhw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id=3D"mwiA">A web browser is not the same thing as a <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLi=
nk" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Search_engine" title=3D"Search en=
gine" id=3D"mwiQ">search engine</a>, though the two are often confused.<sup=
 about=3D"#mwt45" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-13" rel=3D"dc:r=
eferences" typeof=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;r=
ef&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-ref=
erence-text-cite_note-13&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Web_browser#cite_note-13" id=3D"mwig"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D=
"mwiw"><span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwjA">[</span>13<span class=3D"ci=
te-bracket" id=3D"mwjQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=3D"#mwt48" clas=
s=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-14" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"m=
w:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&q=
uot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-=
14&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-=
14" id=3D"mwjg"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwjw"><span class=3D"=
cite-bracket" id=3D"mwkA">[</span>14<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwkQ=
">]</span></span></a></sup> A search engine is a website that provides <a r=
el=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperlink" title=
=3D"Hyperlink" id=3D"mwkg">links</a> to other websites and allows users to =
search for specific resources using a textual <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_query" title=3D"Web query" id=3D"mwkw=
">query</a>. However, web browsers are often used to access search engines,=
 and most modern browsers allow users to access a default search engine dir=
ectly by typing a query into the address bar.<sup about=3D"#mwt51" class=3D=
"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-15" rel=3D"dc:references" typeof=3D"mw:Ex=
tension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;=
:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-15&q=
uot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite_note-15" =
id=3D"mwlA"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwlQ"><span class=3D"cite=
-bracket" id=3D"mwlg">[</span>15<span class=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwlw">]<=
/span></span></a></sup></p>

