wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_security" title=3D"Browser security">Browser sec=
urity</a></div>
<p id=3D"mwAmc">Web browsers are popular targets for <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink"=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hacker" title=3D"Hacker" id=3D"mwAmg=
">hackers</a>, who exploit <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Vulnerability_(computing)" title=3D"Vulnerability (computing)"=
 class=3D"mw-redirect" id=3D"mwAmk">security holes</a> to steal information=
, destroy <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comp=
uter_file" title=3D"Computer file" id=3D"mwAmo">files</a>, and partake in o=
ther <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malware" =
title=3D"Malware" id=3D"mwAms">malicious</a> activities. Browser vendors re=
gularly patch these security holes, so users are strongly encouraged to kee=
p their browser software updated. Other protection measures are <a rel=3D"m=
w:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antivirus_software" title=
=3D"Antivirus software" id=3D"mwAmw">antivirus software</a> and being aware=
 of <a rel=3D"mw:WikiLink" href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_f=
raud" title=3D"Internet fraud" id=3D"mwAm0">scams</a>.<sup about=3D"#mwt174=
" class=3D"mw-ref reference" id=3D"cite_ref-43" rel=3D"dc:references" typeo=
f=3D"mw:Extension/ref" data-mw=3D"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;a=
ttrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite=
_note-43&quot;}}"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser#cite=
_note-43" id=3D"mwAm4"><span class=3D"mw-reflink-text" id=3D"mwAm8"><span c=
lass=3D"cite-bracket" id=3D"mwAnA">[</span>43<span class=3D"cite-bracket" i=
d=3D"mwAnE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

